WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.182
"DHEA: What Is It and What Are Its Benefits?"

00:00:07.243 --> 00:00:10.963
Dehydroepiandrosterone, DHEA,

00:00:10.963 --> 00:00:13.200
is the most abundant
steroid hormone

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.400
circulating in the blood,

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.220
or rather, prohormone.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.220
It's produced largely
by the adrenal glands

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.680
and is then
converted locally in tissues

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.900
into androgens,
male sex hormones,

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.300
or estrogens,
female sex hormones.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.300
DHEA production in the body

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.240
peaks between the ages
of 25 to 35,

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.940
and then gradually
starts to decline

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.160
about 2 percent every year.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.780
By one's 80s, DHEA production
is down about 80 percent

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.060
from peak values
in early adulthood.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:48.000
Cross-sectional studies
found a link

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.100
between low DHEA levels

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.440
and impaired sexual function,

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.420
less vitality,

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.280
depressed mood,

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.740
lower bone mineral density,

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:01.380
and compromised
cognitive performance

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:02.820
in terms of executive function,

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.620
concentration, and memory.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.860
Combined with
interventional studies

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.380
done on rodents
showing a wide range

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:13.320
of beneficial effects,
DHEA was heralded

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:17.220
as an "anti-aging
superhormone panacea,"

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:20.100
even though
rodent adrenal glands

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.960
don't even produce the stuff.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.740
But U.S. DHEA sales grew

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.200
to more than $50 million a year

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.320
on the premise that
replenishing youthful levels

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.300
might have restorative effects.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:37.980
Given the Premarin debacle
with estrogen replacement,

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:42.240
showing that the reversing
of age-related hormonal decline

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.280
can sometimes
do more harm than good,

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.280
clinical trials
were desperately needed.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.580
But because DHEA
can't be patented,

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.320
there's been
little research interest

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.600
among drug companies
to study it.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.080
In fact,
part of its mass appeal is that,

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:01.500
due to a legal loophole,
DHEA is the only steroid

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.020
that's not considered
a controlled substance,

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.900
and therefore is available
over the counter

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.600
as a "dietary supplement,"

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:12.120
rather than
a prescription only drug.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.360
Thankfully,
a series of long-term,

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.820
high-quality randomized
controlled trials

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.340
started to be published
within the last 20 years,

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.640
and early enthusiasm
was replaced

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.860
by a sober skepticism

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:30.000
as the "panacea"
repeatedly failed

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.800
to beat the placebo.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.920
The promised
DHEA fountain of youth

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.420
was drying up.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.040
A review of about two dozen
randomized controlled trials

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.860
of oral DHEA
in postmenopausal women

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:45.960
failed to find evidence
of improvements

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:46.800
in sexual function,

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.540
psychological well-being,

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:50.220
or cognitive performance.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:54.780
However, there may be a role
for intravaginal DHEA

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.280
for vaginal atrophy,

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:57.900
which I covered before.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.740
A meta-analysis
of about two dozen

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:05.760
randomized controlled trials
of DHEA in elderly men

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.240
similarly found no evidence
of benefits for metabolism,

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:12.780
bone health, sexual function,
or quality of life,

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.900
nor does there seem to be
a cognitive benefit.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.420
The only benefit found in men

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:22.320
was a relatively trivial drop
in body fat compared to placebo,

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.620
less than one pound over a span
of eight months.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:27.300
But in women,

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.360
DHEA may benefit fertility.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.440
Fertility in women
starts declining gradually

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.480
but significantly at age 32,

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.000
but then more rapidly
after age 37,

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.000
but DHEA may help.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.880
Side-effects
of taking DHEA supplements

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:47.520
include acne,
oily skin and hair,

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:50.700
and an increase in body hair
and blood levels

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.400
of the cancer-promoting
growth hormone IGF-1.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.920
As with any supplement,
there are concerns

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.480
about quality control issues.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:00.780
Some so-called
"DHEA" supplements

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.280
just blatantly lie

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.560
and have no DHEA whatsoever,

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:08.700
or up to, like,
150 percent of the listed dose.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:10.320
For these and other reasons,

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:13.140
DHEA supplements
are not recommended.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:17.160
Are there natural ways
to boost DHEA,

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.320
for example,
for the fertility benefit?

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:23.280
Lower protein intake is
associated with higher levels,

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.480
and an interventional trial
found increasing fiber intake

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.040
actively raised levels,

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.260
so what about
putting them together?

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:35.820
Enter: "Short-Term Impact
of a Lactovegetarian Diet."

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:39.000
After just five days
on an egg-free vegetarian diet,

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.700
blood levels
of the DHEA precursor rose

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:43.140
nearly 20 percent.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.180
Or you can do it the other way:

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.700
Take those already eating
a plant-based diet

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:49.980
and switch them
to a conventional diet,

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:53.460
and their DHEA drops
up to nearly 20 percent.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.340
The bodies of those
eating plant-based

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:58.560
appear to hold onto
the hormone better,

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.720
less urinary excretion,

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:04.680
which is normally something
you only see in fasting.

